---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
---

<Base title="Motion Effects" description="Complete reference for all vl-effect values — entrance, interaction, continuous, text, and cinema effects.">
  <span class="vl-kicker">Motion</span>

  <h1 class="docs-page-title">Motion Effects</h1>
  <p class="docs-page-lead">
    Named motion presets applied via the <code>vl-effect</code> attribute. All effects are pure CSS —
    no JavaScript involved.
  </p>

  <h2>How Effects Work</h2>
  <p>
    Add <code>vl-effect</code> to any element to apply a preset. Combine with
    <code>vl-timeline</code> to control <em>when</em> the animation plays:
  </p>
  <pre><code>&lt;!-- Plays immediately on page load --&gt;
&lt;h1 vl-effect="fade-up"&gt;Heading&lt;/h1&gt;

&lt;!-- Plays when element enters the viewport --&gt;
&lt;div vl-effect="blur-in" vl-timeline="view"&gt;Content&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;!-- Plays once, stays visible after --&gt;
&lt;div vl-effect="clip-rise" vl-timeline="view" vl-once&gt;One-shot reveal&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;!-- Custom depth and speed --&gt;
&lt;div
  vl-effect="fade-up"
  vl-timeline="view"
  style="--vl-motion-distance: 2.5rem; --vl-motion-duration: 700ms;"&gt;
  Deep, slow reveal
&lt;/div&gt;</code></pre>

  <h2>Entrance Primitives</h2>
  <p>
    Affect the element itself. Best combined with <code>vl-timeline="view"</code> for scroll-driven reveals.
  </p>
  <table>
    <thead>
      <tr><th>Value</th><th>Description</th><th>Default duration</th></tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr>
        <td><code>fade-in</code></td>
        <td>Simple opacity 0 → 1 entrance</td>
        <td><code>--vl-duration-slow</code> (500ms)</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><code>fade-up</code></td>
        <td>Opacity + translateY upward. Workhorse reveal effect.</td>
        <td>500ms</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><code>fade-down</code></td>
        <td>Opacity + translateY downward. Good for dropdowns and menus.</td>
        <td>500ms</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><code>slide-left</code></td>
        <td>Opacity + slide in from the right. Uses <code>--vl-ease-out-soft</code>.</td>
        <td>500ms</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><code>slide-right</code></td>
        <td>Opacity + slide in from the left. Uses <code>--vl-ease-out-soft</code>.</td>
        <td>500ms</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><code>scale-in</code></td>
        <td>Scales from 0.94 with a subtle upward nudge. Uses spring easing.</td>
        <td>500ms</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><code>blur-in</code></td>
        <td>Cinematic blur (14px) dissolve entrance. Dramatic and modern.</td>
        <td><code>--vl-duration-slower</code> (800ms)</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><code>reveal-3d</code></td>
        <td>Perspective rotateX entry — page flip feel.</td>
        <td>500ms</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><code>flow-in</code></td>
        <td>Blur + translate + scale — cinematic combination. Premium look.</td>
        <td>800ms</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><code>clip-rise</code></td>
        <td>Clip-path reveal from bottom. Text feels like it emerges from the page.</td>
        <td>800ms</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><code>tilt-in</code></td>
        <td>Perspective rotateY entry. Great for cards arriving from the side.</td>
        <td>800ms</td>
      </tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <h3>CSS Variable Hooks (Entrance)</h3>
  <pre><code>&lt;div
  vl-effect="fade-up"
  style="
    --vl-motion-duration: 600ms;   /* override speed */
    --vl-motion-distance: 2rem;    /* override travel distance */
    --vl-motion-ease: var(--vl-ease-spring); /* override easing */
  "&gt;
  Custom entrance
&lt;/div&gt;</code></pre>

  <h3>Live Demo</h3>
  <div class="docs-grid-3 docs-section-block">
    <div class="vl-card" vl-effect="fade-up" vl-timeline="view">
      <div class="vl-card__title">fade-up</div>
      <p class="vl-card__body">Opacity + translate Y.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="vl-card" vl-effect="blur-in" vl-timeline="view">
      <div class="vl-card__title">blur-in</div>
      <p class="vl-card__body">Cinematic blur dissolve.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="vl-card" vl-effect="reveal-3d" vl-timeline="view">
      <div class="vl-card__title">reveal-3d</div>
      <p class="vl-card__body">Perspective rotateX entry.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <h2>Interaction Effects</h2>
  <p>
    Applied to interactive elements. These respond to user hover — no timeline needed.
  </p>
  <table>
    <thead>
      <tr><th>Value</th><th>Trigger</th><th>Description</th></tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr>
        <td><code>hover-lift</code></td>
        <td><code>:hover</code></td>
        <td>Translates up 4px + floating shadow. Classic card hover.</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><code>hover-glow</code></td>
        <td><code>:hover</code></td>
        <td>Adds a primary-colored glow shadow ring. Great for media embeds.</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><code>underline-expand</code></td>
        <td><code>:hover</code></td>
        <td>Expanding underline grows from center. Elegant nav link effect.</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><code>icon-shift</code></td>
        <td><code>:hover</code></td>
        <td>Last child (icon/arrow) shifts 4px on hover. Use on inline elements with an icon sibling.</td>
      </tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <pre><code>&lt;!-- hover-lift on a card --&gt;
&lt;div class="vl-card" vl-effect="hover-lift"&gt;
  Hover me
&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;!-- underline-expand on a nav link --&gt;
&lt;a href="/about" vl-effect="underline-expand"&gt;About&lt;/a&gt;

&lt;!-- icon-shift on a CTA --&gt;
&lt;a href="/docs" vl-effect="icon-shift"&gt;
  Read the docs
  &lt;svg aria-hidden="true"&gt;&lt;!-- arrow icon --&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;
&lt;/a&gt;</code></pre>

  <p>
    <strong>Touch devices:</strong> Hover effects automatically disable via <code>@media (hover: none)</code>.
  </p>

  <h2>State Effects</h2>
  <p>
    Used with toggled elements like accordions, drawers, and panels. Typically paired with
    <code>[open]</code>, a class toggle, or <code>:checked</code>:
  </p>
  <table>
    <thead>
      <tr><th>Value</th><th>Description</th></tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr>
        <td><code>accordion</code></td>
        <td>Height + opacity transition for disclosure panels. Use with <code>interpolate-size: allow-keywords</code> (included in Velora reset).</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><code>drawer</code></td>
        <td>Transform + opacity + <code>visibility</code> transition with <code>transition-behavior: allow-discrete</code>.</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><code>panel-swap</code></td>
        <td>Opacity + quick transform for tab panel swaps.</td>
      </tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <pre><code>&lt;!-- Use the .vl-accordion component for a complete implementation --&gt;
&lt;details class="vl-accordion"&gt;
  &lt;summary&gt;Question&lt;/summary&gt;
  &lt;div class="vl-accordion__content"&gt;Answer text&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/details&gt;</code></pre>

  <h2>Continuous / Ambient Effects</h2>
  <p>
    Loop indefinitely. Use to add life to decorative elements, loading states, or ambient backgrounds.
    Always respect <code>prefers-reduced-motion</code> — wrap with the media query if adding ambient
    effects to content-critical elements.
  </p>
  <table>
    <thead>
      <tr><th>Value</th><th>Loop duration</th><th>Description</th></tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td><code>shimmer</code></td><td>2.5s</td><td>Background shimmer sweep. Use on skeleton loaders or accent lines. Requires <code>background-size: 200% auto</code> and a gradient background.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>float</code></td><td>5.5s</td><td>Gentle vertical bob. Great for hero illustrations.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>glow-breathe</code></td><td>3.5s</td><td>Pulsing box-shadow. Use on live indicators or accent dots.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>wobble</code></td><td>2.8s</td><td>Tilt oscillation (±3deg). Attention-grabbing but subtle.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>orbit</code></td><td>14s</td><td>Circular orbit — full 360deg spin. For orbital icons or decorative rings.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>rock</code></td><td>4s</td><td>Wider tilt oscillation (±6deg). More playful than wobble.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>morph</code></td><td>8s</td><td>Organic border-radius morphing. Use on blobs and abstract shapes.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>elastic-in</code></td><td>0.7s</td><td>Springy scale-in entrance. One-shot spring pop, not a loop.</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <pre><code>&lt;!-- Floating hero illustration --&gt;
&lt;img src="hero-visual.png" alt="" vl-effect="float" /&gt;

&lt;!-- Breathing glow on a live badge --&gt;
&lt;span class="vl-badge" vl-effect="glow-breathe"&gt;Live&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;!-- Shimmer skeleton --&gt;
&lt;div
  vl-effect="shimmer"
  style="
    height: 1rem;
    border-radius: var(--vl-radius-md);
    background: linear-gradient(
      90deg,
      var(--vl-bg-surface-elevated) 0%,
      var(--vl-bg-surface) 50%,
      var(--vl-bg-surface-elevated) 100%
    );
    background-size: 200% auto;
  "&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;</code></pre>

  <h2>Text Reveal Effects</h2>
  <p>
    Clip-path-based reveals designed for headlines. Apply to heading elements for editorial impact.
  </p>
  <table>
    <thead>
      <tr><th>Value</th><th>Direction</th><th>Description</th></tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td><code>text-reveal</code></td><td>Left → right</td><td>Horizontal clip sweep across text</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>text-reveal-up</code></td><td>Bottom → top</td><td>Text rises up from a clipped baseline</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>text-reveal-down</code></td><td>Top → bottom</td><td>Text falls into view from above</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <pre><code>&lt;h1 vl-effect="text-reveal-up" vl-timeline="view"&gt;
  Premium interfaces start here
&lt;/h1&gt;</code></pre>

  <h2>Cinema / Scroll Effects</h2>
  <p>
    These effects use <code>animation-timeline: view(block)</code> internally. They are inherently
    scroll-driven and do <em>not</em> need <code>vl-timeline="view"</code> added separately.
  </p>
  <table>
    <thead>
      <tr><th>Value</th><th>Range</th><th>Description</th></tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr>
        <td><code>cinema-zoom</code></td>
        <td><code>entry 0% exit 100%</code></td>
        <td>Slow zoom + focus shift tied to scroll position. Ken Burns feel for hero images.</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><code>parallax</code></td>
        <td><code>cover</code></td>
        <td>Vertical parallax shift as element scrolls through viewport.</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><code>typewriter</code></td>
        <td>N/A (time-based)</td>
        <td>CSS typewriter effect with blinking caret. Configure with <code>--vl-type-duration</code> and <code>--vl-type-steps</code>.</td>
      </tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <pre><code>&lt;!-- Cinema zoom on a hero image --&gt;
&lt;img src="hero.jpg" alt="Hero" vl-effect="cinema-zoom" /&gt;

&lt;!-- Parallax section background --&gt;
&lt;div vl-effect="parallax"&gt;
  &lt;img src="bg.jpg" alt="" /&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;!-- Typewriter with custom timing --&gt;
&lt;p
  vl-effect="typewriter"
  style="--vl-type-duration: 3s; --vl-type-steps: 40;"&gt;
  Building the future of motion design.
&lt;/p&gt;</code></pre>

  <h2>Speed Modifier</h2>
  <p>Override the animation duration category with <code>vl-speed</code>:</p>
  <pre><code>&lt;div vl-effect="fade-up" vl-speed="fast"&gt;Quick reveal&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div vl-effect="flow-in" vl-speed="slow"&gt;Slow dramatic reveal&lt;/div&gt;</code></pre>
  <table>
    <thead>
      <tr><th>Value</th><th>Duration</th></tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td><code>fast</code></td><td><code>--vl-duration-fast</code> (150ms)</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>normal</code></td><td><code>--vl-duration-normal</code> (300ms)</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>slow</code></td><td><code>--vl-duration-slow</code> (500ms)</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <h2>Depth Modifier</h2>
  <p>Control the translation distance with <code>vl-depth</code>:</p>
  <pre><code>&lt;div vl-effect="fade-up" vl-depth="1"&gt;Subtle — 0.75rem travel&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div vl-effect="fade-up" vl-depth="4"&gt;Dramatic — 4rem travel&lt;/div&gt;</code></pre>
  <table>
    <thead>
      <tr><th>Value</th><th><code>--vl-motion-distance</code></th></tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td><code>1</code></td><td>0.75rem</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>2</code></td><td>1.5rem</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>3</code></td><td>2.5rem</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>4</code></td><td>4rem</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <h2>Accessibility</h2>
  <p>
    All <code>vl-effect</code> animations automatically disable via:
  </p>
  <pre><code>@media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) &#123;
  [vl-effect] &#123;
    animation: none !important;
  &#125;
&#125;</code></pre>
  <p>
    Interaction effects (<code>hover-lift</code>, <code>hover-glow</code>) also disable on touch devices
    via <code>@media (hover: none)</code>.
  </p>

  <h2>Browser Support</h2>
  <p>
    Entrance, interaction, state, and continuous effects work in all modern browsers (Chrome 89+, Firefox 90+, Safari 15+).
  </p>
  <p>
    Scroll-driven effects (<code>cinema-zoom</code>, <code>parallax</code>, <code>vl-timeline="view"</code>)
    require Chrome 115+ / Edge 115+. A graceful fallback is included via
    <code>@supports not (animation-timeline: view(block))</code> — these elements simply appear in their
    final state on unsupported browsers.
  </p>
</Base>
